  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Huangmei opera (Huangmei xi) Chinese regional opera tradition originating in the late nineteenth century in the Huangmei county of Hubei province and developing through the early-twentieth century in Anhui province (especially Anqing region) into one of the five major Chinese opera traditions. Distinguished from the elite kunqu and jingju by accessible vernacular Anhui-and-Hubei dialect language, simple rural-folk melodic vocabulary (developed from tea-picking and rice-planting work songs), and more naturalistic theatrical-realism in staging. The Tianxianpei (\"Heavenly Match\") play is the canonical type-specimen. The post-1949 Anhui Provincial Huangmei Opera Theatre consolidated the modern repertoire.",
